{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And a wind went.</b> Second day." "<b>And he cut.</b> Like גזי נזרך (cut off your locks) and from the root of וגז צאנך (and your sheep's shearing)." "The meaning of <b>ויגז</b> is that they were at the edge of the sea, numerous as sand, and behold he sheared from them. And the word ויגז is of the doubled [roots], like ויחם בשר הילד (and the child's flesh grew warm)." "<b>ויטש.</b> Like ויפרוש (and he spread). And the meaning is like an abandoned thing that has no strength to turn away, and likewise והנם נטושים על פני כל הארץ (and behold they are spread over all the earth)." "<b>Around the camp.</b> Moreover, the meaning is that they were as if true [spread] in every place, high or low."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:17:20.839199383Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}